WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.700
Hello.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.860
What's your name?

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.990
I'm Mikhail, but you can call me Misha!

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.330
Your name isn't Mikhail anymore.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.130
It's Number 71!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.550
We're nothing more
than Moreau's guinea pigs!

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:49.020
Ow!

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:16.280
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.820
--No!

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.620
--Doctor. The test subject is too young.
--No!

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.410
He won't survive much more.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:30.500
Well, we can bring in
the next child in that case.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.550
I'm so close to creating what I want.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.840
Humans that can serve as a link!

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.930
Help me, big brother!

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.640
Help!

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.890
Big brother!

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.900
Doctor!

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.070
I will do it.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:05.700
Use me instead of that little brat!

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:11.540
Doctor, let me help you
achieve your noble purpose!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.380
How marvelous!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.380
Has there ever been
a single child like you

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.220
who's willingly cooperated
in my experiments?!

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.850
No, there hasn't!

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.680
But of course, Number 69!
What a marvelous idea!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.100
Together we shall draw one step closer

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.730
to the great wisdom of
the vampires and the world!

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.820
Thank you, big brother.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.790
I was wondering if I could
sleep with you tonight.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.340
You're so warm.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.260
Ta-da!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:09.100
My experiment has entered its final phase!

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:14.230
I'll use this to link you two
to <i>The Books of Vanitas</i>.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.520
<i>The Books of Vanitas</i>?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.730
Yes, that's an excellent
question, Number 69!

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:24.450
These books were created by
the Vampire of the Blue Moon!

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:28.120
But they're even more legendary
than that legendary vampire!

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.540
They're powered by
a special form of astermite.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.920
They pack sorcery, alchemy, and many other
technologies into miniature machines.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.130
They're analytical engines in book form!

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:43.170
Supposedly, one can use these books

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.680
to easily alter the World Formula!

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.760
Supposedly?

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.730
That's right! They won't open,
no matter how I try!

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:59.940
From what I've heard, only members
of the Blue Moon Clan can do that!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.610
Isn't that awful?!

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.280
Isn't it so unfair!

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.240
And so...

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:17.420
I decided to transform you two into
quasi members of the Blue Moon Clan!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.460
What?

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.550
I wish to make human switches,

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.260
their only purpose being
to open the books!

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:28.260
You know that blue fluid
I often inject you with?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.640
Do you know what it is?

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.680
Tick.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.810
Tick.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.640
Tick.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:37.560
Sorry, time's up! You lose!

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.520
Prepare to be amazed!

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.320
It's none other than

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:45.690
the Vampire of the Blue Moon's blood!

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.610
Oh, dear, what's wrong?

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:51.830
You're so startled,
you've been rendered speechless?!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.080
I know how you feel!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.160
Big brother?

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.790
To prevent a fatal rejection response,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:01.750
I injected you ever so gradually
with the vampire's blood

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:05.960
along with special medicine.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:09.470
Big brother!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:14.310
Didn't you notice your wounds
have been healing faster than before?

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.310
You've been elevated one step
beyond human bounds!

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.980
You are now a very special kind of being!

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.900
I am going to kill you.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.450
I have the two <i>Books of Vanitas</i>
and the two of you!

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.570
Perfect, don't you think?

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.790
No!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:39.960
That hurts!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.330
Stop it!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.710
I'm going to kill you!

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:46.090
I swear I'll murder every last one of you!

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:50.550
How dare you do this to me?!

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.600
Oh, right, I forgot to mention one thing.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.810
Once I activate this machine,

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:00.440
the shock of linking to the books
may turn you both into vegetables.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.480
So let me express my
gratitude while I can.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.650
Thank you, Numbers 69 and 71.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.700
I will never forget you!

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.340
What's happening?!

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.220
What the blazes?!

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:56.580
Big brother!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.120
Dear me.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:09.590
Some humans come up
with the most ludicrous ideas.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:17.680
Now then, I think I've done
quite enough damage.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.520
I must go before the Chasseurs arrive.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.810
No, don't go!

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.060
Take us with you!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.950
Take us, too.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.330
Oh, my.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:51.340
Well, this wouldn't have
happened if not for me.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:57.550
How could he be so cruel?

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:00.470
They are but children.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.980
Mikhail.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.350
Well, what will you do?

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.610
Will you, too...

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.820
...come with me?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.160
Big brother.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:52.270
We've gone far enough.
We should be safe for now.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:56.320
We're still not that far from town.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.570
The Chasseurs will be here before you--

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:00.320
No, they won't.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:05.290
That researcher... Moreau, was it?

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:11.290
He was engaged in acts
banned by Church teachings.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.380
When the Chasseur's come running
and find what he's done,

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:19.430
they will scramble to control
the damage rather than pursue us.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:26.230
And most of the researchers that
were there have likely been slain.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:31.730
Now that we're safe and sound,
I'd like for us to introduce ourselves.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.190
--My name is Mikhail!
But you can call me Misha!

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.940
--Wait, Mikhail!
--My name is Mikhail!
But you can call me Misha!

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:37.990
Misha?

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.740
Yes?!

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:44.450
I regret to say I have no name
with which to introduce myself.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.700
Or perhaps it would be best to say

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:51.000
I have yet no name
with which I'm satisfied.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:07.020
I am the Vampire of the Blue Moon.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:16.190
There are some who call me Vanitas.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:18.030
You're beautiful.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:24.990
The Vampire... of the Blue Moon?

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.370
Big brother?!

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:33.630
You went straight for my eyes.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.800
I take it you were among the
children the Chasseurs were training.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.470
Have you taken us away to devour us?!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.010
Blue blood?

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.390
You're mistaken.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.970
Then what?!

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:54.310
Have you come to reclaim your
blood that they injected into us?

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.690
I took you

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.360
because you asked for my help.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:08.790
N-No. I never...

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:11.120
...asked...

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:12.670
Big brother!

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.630
Dear me.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:30.430
My big brother's awake!

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:39.110
You need not worry.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.900
This is the home of a human with
whom I've been long acquainted.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.030
Don't be absurd.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:50.330
Why would a vampire be
acquainted with a human?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.080
It's not unheard of.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.250
Those who come from a long line
of alchemists or sorcerers

00:12:55.250 --> 00:13:00.380
have always had an affinity for
vampires rather than the Church.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.930
Your exhaustion took a toll
once you let your guard down.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:09.760
Were you not always braced to
defend Misha at a moment's notice?

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:13.350
But now, all you need do is rest.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:20.860
I will sing you a lullaby
so you may better sleep.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.070
I want to sing, too.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.240
Very well.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:30.700
What sorts of songs did
your mother sing to you?

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.870
What?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.370
Hm? Oh...

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:38.750
You called out "Mother"
many times in your delirium.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.210
That's a lie.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.470
No, it's not.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.090
Yes, it is.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:50.640
There's no way I said that. After all...

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.310
My mother died when I was born.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:59.150
I would never call for her.
I would never...

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.080
Big brother...

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:28.300
So then...

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:33.510
...you lived alone with your father?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.890
It wasn't just the two of us.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.060
There were others.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.940
Others?

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:46.990
My father was born to a good family,
and he became a doctor.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.660
But he abandoned them
after meeting my mother,

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:53.580
who was part of a traveling
show that came to town.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.700
A bold move.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.910
What's a traveling show?

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.670
It's like a circus.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.540
It wasn't as respectable as that.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:08.590
I got the feeling my father
didn't care for them too much.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:12.640
We went to all sorts
of places with the show.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.890
You don't say?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:18.810
They told me I looked
a lot like my mother.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.520
I see. Then she was a beauty.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.940
I think so, too!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:28.360
But she died because of me.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:33.660
My father should have
hated me for that, but...

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.910
When the vampires attacked,

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:43.380
Father died protecting me!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.920
Why?

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.710
I want to ask him that, but I can't.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:52.010
I'll never know the answer.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:57.260
Do you hate vampires?

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.100
Of course I do!

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.810
I want to wipe them
from the face of the earth!

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.690
I want to make this world clean again!

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:08.110
That's why I vowed to
live my life as a Chasseur!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.820
I...

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:16.950
They often experimented on vampires
they brought to Moreau's lab.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:21.540
At first, I felt they were
getting their just deserts.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.960
But gradually,

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:28.800
I came to realize humans are
the most terrifying monsters of all.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:39.310
Would it have not been easy for one
like you to escape from such a place?

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:42.020
So why did you stay?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:48.360
Moreau led the Chasseurs to
believe that I had died in battle.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.400
He killed a stranger and
passed his body off as mine.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:58.490
And he told me he would simply
obtain another child if I left.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:03.790
So I felt I had no choice
but to remain there.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:12.090
I didn't want to think about any of it.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.220
I didn't understand.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:17.180
And I still don't.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:20.850
What am I to do now?

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:25.310
I have learned something.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:30.690
You are a truly kind child.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.620
No, I'm not.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:41.740
Yes, you are.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:46.710
No, I'm not at all like that. I'm...

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.430
Big brother?

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:02.890
Forget what I said!

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:08.560
Forget every last word I said yesterday.
Wipe it clean from your brain!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:12.190
Yesterday? From when to when?

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:14.230
From the moment we left the lab?

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:19.780
Or from the time you feverishly yelled,
"No, no, no!" while you cried?

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.660
Just forget it, already!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.790
Oh, you're awake? Good timing.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.910
I just finished making breakfast.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:30.000
Breakfast? I'm starving!

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:37.420
Now, eat up! You need all
the nutrients you can get.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:44.520
You really <i>are</i> trying
to kill us, aren't you?

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.060
Why would you say that?

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:49.560
What is this sludge-like toxic waste?!

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.060
It's called soup.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.610
I added lots of medicinal herbs
so it would be good for you.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:58.570
And I just freshly drew this milk.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:01.320
Why is it all black and disgusting?!

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.870
And this room is filthy!
It's full of spider webs and rats!

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.620
I didn't notice yesterday.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:11.130
But if you're staying in someone's home,
keep it clean! Unbelievable!

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.920
Fine. Do everything yourself.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.720
Stop sulking, you big baby!

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:26.560
How's that?!

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.640
Yummy!

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.770
Oh my, I am utterly defeated.

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:36.280
You're a most magnificent child.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.900
More, please!

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:47.540
There is no point hiding it.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:52.710
You both will likely die before too long.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:55.920
It may be in a month, six months,

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:59.670
or even five years from now. Who can say?

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:04.260
But that day will come.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:08.560
Moreau's experiments have forced
your bodies beyond what is human.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:13.400
You are now getting closer
to the race of vampires.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:17.900
But your bodies waver
precariously on a razor's edge.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:22.070
At any moment, the balance may tip,
and your current state

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:26.240
will be in unbearable conflict
with the natural order.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:32.040
It is then that your bodies
will begin to break down.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:37.420
Come with me if you
have nowhere else to turn.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:43.470
Together we shall seek a way to save you.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:53.980
Father, am I going to die?

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:59.780
There is one way to save you
that I have yet to mention.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:04.320
I could make you members of my clan.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.870
But that...

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:10.660
It's not something I wanted to resort to.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:16.250
I want to join your clan, Father.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:22.340
After all, it means the three of us
can be together forever, doesn't it?

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:26.340
I don't ever want to be
a member of your clan,

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.930
even if it meant dying tomorrow.

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:33.850
I want to continue being
human until the end.

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:47.780
You finally made it,

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:49.660
big brother!

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.880
What have you done to him?

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:05.010
"Blue Night"

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:41.500
"Tears like Rain"
